# Bounds, for `proved.mm`.
#
# A least upper bound over the reals is a set, which a define naming one
# asks of its value (`gsupex`).

$( Bounds: a least upper bound over the reals is a set. $)

# `gsupex`: |- sup ( A , RR , < ) e. _V. A least upper bound in the reals is
# a set, as any term is that the page writes (`rules::SETHOOD`): `supex`,
# with `ltso` the order it is taken in.
lemma gsupex
  |- sup ( A , RR , < ) e. _V
  1 ltso |- < Or RR
  2 supex 1 |- sup ( A , RR , < ) e. _V
